-# Builds Playnck for Windows and Linux on their own native runners
-# (electron-builder can't reliably cross-build a real Fedora RPM from
-# Windows, or a trustworthy NSIS installer from Linux, so each
-# platform gets its own GitHub-hosted machine instead of one runner
-# trying to do both) and, for an actual release, combines both
-# outputs into a single GitHub Release.
-#
-# Three jobs:
-#   build-windows  -> Playnck-<version> Setup.exe
-#   build-linux    -> playnck-<version>.x86_64.rpm
-#   publish        -> downloads both, uploads them to one release,
-#                      publishes it (see build-scripts/publish-release.js
-#                      for why this is a separate step instead of
-#                      letting each build job publish for itself)
-#
-# build-windows/build-linux always run, on every push/PR against main,
-# as a "does this still build" check — the fast, cheap part of "the
-# release is built on the correct operating system" from the project
-# brief. publish only runs for an actual release: a pushed v* tag, or
-# manually via "Run workflow" above.
-#
-# No secrets to configure: publish only ever needs to write releases
-# to this same repository, which the workflow's automatic
-# GITHUB_TOKEN already covers (see the `permissions:` block below).
-# A personal GH_TOKEN is only needed for running `npm run release`
-# from a developer's own machine, exactly as before this workflow
-# existed.
 
 name: Release
 
